Well, actually, I really like this idea, though I think it would be hard
to implement and wickedly hard to balance. Currently, you can only use
quest artifacts of your alignment or role. It would be interesting if "of
your role" gave you more choices. On the other hand, this would introduce
many more Quest Artifacts to the game, making even more ultrapowerful
items that players could wish for... of course, when was the last time
you wished for the Heart of Ahriman? Maybe it wouldn't be so bad...

I actually really like Chromatic Dragon scale mail, not scales, because
it would give neutral cavemen the ability to play a wishless illiterate
with DSM (and without a bonesfile). That makes that conduct set a little
easier, but so do monk resistances for foodless and priests for atheist,
so I don't see that as a problem. The problem with this idea, I think,
is coming up with a reasonable set of artifacts and plot justifications
(thin or otherwise) for every class/alignment set. I think that doing
this while maintaining balance would be very difficult; it likely could
be done, but I don't think anyone is going to. :)

Still, I like the idea.

